<title>USA: Capital EPS in line with lower expectations.</title>
<headline>Capital EPS in line with lower expectations.</headline>
<dateline>FALLS CHURCH, Va. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capital One Financial Corp said Tuesday its net second-quarter earnings of $39.4 million, or $0.58 a share, were in line with management's lowered expectations.</p>
<p>The bank posted earnings of $38.2 million, or $0.57 a share, in the second quarter of last year.</p>
<p>In the first quarter of this year, the bank's earnings were $42.5 million, or $0.63 a share,</p>
<p>The bank attributed its second-quarter results to higher balance attrition and lower delinquency rates, which provided less fee income.</p>
</text>
